# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Clock buffers and their muxes (2026-10-26), from designs/kv260_cmt_char:
# 100 random specimens (BUFGCE, BUFGCE_DIV, BUFGCTRL, MMCM, PLL on random
# CMT_L sites, Vivado characterisation only; 40 of them weighted towards
# BUFGCTRL and BUFGCE_DIV). Generated by emit_cmt.py from
# mux.py (per-mux: the bits that are a function of the selected input, the
# CLK_CMT_MUX_*_ENC selects being encoded) and solve.py (site attributes).
# Only inputs seen in two or more instances are here. The MUX_16_ENC muxes
# are enc.py's, below.
#
# Regenerated 2026-10-26 with the 40 kv260_mmcm_char specimens pooled in
# (mux.py --min-frame 4: frames 0-3 hold the MMCM/PLL registers, written by
# the drp.corrections block further down). The extra data dropped bits some
# lines had claimed by coincidence. The BUFGCE <- MMCM/PLL output selects are
# bufg_enc.py's, below. Checked over the 400 kv260_cmt_char and 160
# kv260_mmcm_char CMT_L instances (frames 4-11): no bit predicted that Vivado
# left clear. Still unexplained: a few bits beside the BUFGCE_DIV/BUFGCTRL
# sites (e.g. <frame>_1547, _1527-1530, in 20-30 cmt_char instances), and the
# VDISTR pips that were seen only once.
#
# A chain that is always used whole (MUX_2TO1 <- MUX_16_ENC_k and
# HROUTE_0_k <- that MUX_2TO1) carries the same bits on each pip.
# BUFGCE_X0Y<k>: CE_TYPE SYNC and IN_USE set nothing; IS_I_INVERTED sets
# nothing either (Vivado absorbs it upstream), so nextpnr refuses it.
# BUFGCE_DIVIDE is DIVIDE-1 in three bits (field.py).
# BUFGCE_X0Y0 was never sampled (track 0 is the PS clock's in every
# specimen); its two bits follow the pattern of the other 23 sites (groups
# of six share a frame pair; frames alternate; bit steps every two sites).
CMT_L.BUFGCE_X0Y0.CE_TYPE.ASYNC add-feature 06_1542  # inferred
CMT_L.BUFGCE_X0Y0.IS_CE_INVERTED add-feature 07_1548  # inferred
CMT_L.BUFGCE_DIV_X0Y0.BUFGCE_DIVIDE.D2 add-feature 06_1545
